{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/21622-when-have-you-set-your-mummy-the-curse-chronicles","id":21622,"title":"When have you set your Mummy: The Curse chronicles?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-02T07:50:18-08:00","id":21622,"title":"When have you set your Mummy: The Curse chronicles?","content":"I'm interested to hear the time periods in which you've set your Mummy chronicles, and why you chose those time periods in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T10:03:16-08:00","id":21735,"title":"","content":"I haven't started any Mummy chronicles as such, but the Arisen have made their presence felt in a modern day chronicle in Peru, and in a 3013 AD chronicle.<br /> Mummies entombed in orbiting space stations or forlorn asteroids seemed like a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T13:57:51-08:00","id":21876,"title":"","content":"I've recently set a mummy game during 1942 as the German forces led by Erwin Rommel pushed into north africa and the Nazi occultists followed in their wake pillaging tombs. Its still within living memory, well documented and so easy to research. It was one of the first things that popped into my head as we were sitting around wondering what to do one sunday and there is a simple uncomplicated fun to be had apparently in unleashing tier 3 utterances against the third reich. seemed easy to run a session that explored the more superficial and obvious aspects of (un)life as an arisen without having to worry about the underlying themes and mood to much (which can wait untill ive written a much better story for the current sothic turn in istanbul)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T14:37:58-08:00","id":22600,"title":"","content":"While they've thusfar been flashbacks, three of my settings in his history include Camelot, the wild west, and early hokkaido. he was quite the nomad. though i will also say a space opera with mummies does sound pretty awesome. itd have some stargate vibes, and mesh to the theory of shaniatu being aliens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T05:56:19-08:00","id":23088,"title":"","content":"My current chronicle is set in Washington, DC circa 2011 about 9 months befoe the the 2012 Sothic Turn (which serves as climax to the chronicle).<br /> <br /> My next mummy game will be set in 1910 Cairo Egypt and will involve the creation of the cult for my current story (so essentially it will be a flashback story to how the cult ended up in Washington, DC USA and how the cult was formed by the Arisen). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T05:54:14-08:00","id":23701,"title":"","content":"I'm planning on having my PC wake up for a short adventure in the late 1980s, followed by a Sothic awakening in 2009 or so. Before those she had a Descent in the early 20th century, which is all her history I have planned so far","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T08:53:03-08:00","id":23780,"title":"","content":"Trying to work on The Frozen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T10:21:45-08:00","id":23822,"title":"","content":"I'm in the development stages of a French Revolution Mummy game. I think this era could work well as either a stand alone chronicle, or as a prequel to a present day game.<br /> <br /> The eternal servant wakes up, to discover that the lower castes are rising up against their leaders. Apart from the direct challenges of dodging revolutionaries and protecting ones cult in a world where the aristos are pariah, on an existential level how does the mummy deal with the revolution? Is she appalled by the actions of the revolutionaries? How dare they rise up againt their betters?! But then again, if mere mortals can do it, can the mummy not do the same? &quot;The secret of freedom lies in educating people, whereas the secret of tyranny is in keeping them ignorant&quot; Robspierre said. Are the Shan'iatu and the Judges deliberately keeping their servants ignorant? Can they in turn be overthrown? Can the mummy decide its own destiny? <br /> <br /> Those are the questions that makes me believe French Revolution Mummy could be an awesome setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T11:40:23-08:00","id":23862,"title":"","content":"My Chronicle is set in Mumbai, in nested flashbacks - the whole Chronicle so far is a flashback within a framing story set in the 22nd Century. We've had a story during the Partition of India, and a story in the 2012 Sothic Turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T07:32:04-08:00","id":54648,"title":"","content":"I haven't run or played Mummy yet (to my dismay), but I have ideas in my head for a space opera game with some pretty high-xp Arisen being woken up several decades after humanity discovered alien ruins on Mars and came into contact with the galactic community.<br /> <br /> And by that I mean Mass Effect crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:35:45-08:00","id":54752,"title":"","content":"My French Revolution game fell flat due to a lack of interest in the French Revolution by my players (sacrebleu). I will instead be running the Avarice Chroncile for them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In other words, hurry up and publish the next book in the series, dammit!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T11:33:24-08:00","id":54784,"title":"","content":"At the opening of chronicle, my PCs are in Paris, France in January of 1559. I'm planning on skipping forward through time, and sometimes backtracking to fill in Descents that have become interesting through Memory increases or story developments.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, is there a section of this forum for &quot;Actual Play&quot; threads?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T00:10:29-08:00","id":55987,"title":"","content":"There's a play by post forum. My current game is set in the Third Turn, Constantinople (and the Byzantine Empire) as the Arisen take it upon themselves to hunt down apotheosis-seeking heretics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T06:49:29-08:00","id":56714,"title":"","content":"It may or may not contradict existing canon, but in my Mummyverse, the Heretic (rather like Saulot in owod) learned his secrets in the far east. The way I run my secret history ********SPOILERS********** is that sometime before/during the first Turn, many Mummies were appaled by their condition and traveled East, seeking freedom. In my chronicle, the Heretic is not the first Mummy to attain Apotheiosis, merely the most famous and outspoken. I'm using the Eight Immortals myth to create eight Mummies of various sorts and mindsets who acheived apotheiosis before Buddha was born. Thus, in addition to the Dreams of Avarice, mummies seeking aptheiosis in my game often travel to India, Tibet, Nepal, and other north and far eastern areas instinctually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:09:22-08:00","id":56724,"title":"","content":"You can include spoiler tags by typing [spoiler.] [/spoiler.] minus the . at each end of what you want to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:13:53-08:00","id":56726,"title":"","content":"Sadly, on my mobile device, that sort of stuff typically backfires. It even forces everything I say into one paragraph :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T21:53:38-08:00","id":64586,"title":"","content":"I'm running a Mummy chronicle set at the southmost point of the continental US in the Rio Grande Valley. Lots of stuff to draw from in the area from a confirmed human-sacrifice cult in the 80s to the the headquarters of the Gulf cartel being located right across the border. It also helps that I have family from the place and am drawing on stuff I've seen. Tis been a lot of fun, particularly with the cults/mummy interactions since the cultist had no idea what their gods were going to be like when awoken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><a href=\"http://maidrpg.com\" target=\"_blank\">Maids</a> </span><span style=\"color:#404040\">+ Exalted = <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/maidzalt\" target=\"_blank\">Maid the RPG: Exalted Edition</a>! More chaos than you can shake an artifact feather duster at! Also, my <a href=\"https://www.obsidianportal.com/profile/Teleute\" target=\"_blank\">Obsidian Portal page</a>.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":1853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1853-teleute","user":"teleute","date":". 02-04-2014, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1853-teleute","name":"teleute","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1853_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T06:24:56-08:00","id":64795,"title":"","content":"I'm planning on a &quot;Let's explore the obvious, superficial trappings of mummies in a fun, loose environment by protecting a labyrinthine tomb from Brendan Frasier and Rachel Weisz in the late 1920s/30s in Egypt&quot;.<br /> <br /> Very early planning stage. Mostly because I'm already running two games and that's about my limit. Plus I don't want to switch gears from <i>Blood and Smoke</i> to NWoD 1.0, and don't have the patience or experience for doing that sort of conversion work right now. Plus none of my players are familiar with NWoD of either &quot;edition&quot; so I don't want to throw that at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T15:59:10-08:00","id":65203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/21622-when-have-you-set-your-mummy-the-curse-chronicles?p=64795#post64795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm planning on a &quot;Let's explore the obvious, superficial trappings of mummies in a fun, loose environment by protecting a labyrinthine tomb from Brendan Frasier and Rachel Weisz in the late 1920s/30s in Egypt&quot;.<br /> <br /> Very early planning stage. Mostly because I'm already running two games and that's about my limit. Plus I don't want to switch gears from <i>Blood and Smoke</i> to NWoD 1.0, and don't have the patience or experience for doing that sort of conversion work right now. Plus none of my players are familiar with NWoD of either &quot;edition&quot; so I don't want to throw that at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm this guy basically. I know some people have done a little conversion work for Mummy but it's not all complete and an entire overhaul is too much work for me to do, even just running one game.<br /> <br /> I wish the Dark Eras source-book would come out sooner because it would just fit my premise so perfectly. My campaign is basically, &quot;How did all those old/remade Mummy films work if they were in the Mummy: the Curse world?&quot; Complete with reincarnated lovers, Scorpion Kings, and encounters with Dracula's brides, Frankenstein's monster, and wolf-men","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T22:25:03-08:00","id":65417,"title":"","content":"Yeah the 20s/30s and generally the Time of the Egyptomania, is an interesting Period for the Game. BTW does anybody know ,wich Time-period the Mummys will actualy get in Dark Eras ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T16:32:23-08:00","id":66051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeadGuy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/21622-when-have-you-set-your-mummy-the-curse-chronicles?p=65417#post65417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW does anybody know ,wich Time-period the Mummys will actualy get in Dark Eras ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...I kinda implied which period it would be in my post, where I mentioned how I was anticipating the release of Dark Eras. The period that Mummy will take place in <i>is</i> the early 20th century <i>because</i> it's the &quot;time of Egyptomania&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, lucky for you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T21:28:01-08:00","id":66245,"title":"","content":"well thats cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T17:39:55-08:00","id":323988,"title":"","content":"Tenochtitlan, 1474.<br /> <br /> Gives me an occasion to finally get some use out of both Mummy and Shadows of Mexico.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T23:50:39-08:00","id":324250,"title":"","content":"Just started a chronicle (me as a player), and we're in the Indus Valley Civilisation. Or rather, we'll be <i>building </i>the Indus Valley Civilisation. From what we can tell, Irem fell as little as a year ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T07:49:23-08:00","id":324513,"title":"","content":"I would complain that as the timeline goes that makes absolutely no sense (the first mummies woke up 1461 years, plus or minus a century, after the fall of the Nameless Empire).<br /> <br /> But that would be dumb, because you're doing something as awesome as <i>building the Indus Valley Civilization.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T09:32:35-08:00","id":324587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/21622-when-have-you-set-your-mummy-the-curse-chronicles?p=66051#post66051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well...I kinda implied which period it would be in my post, where I mentioned how I was anticipating the release of Dark Eras. The period that Mummy will take place in <i>is</i> the early 20th century <i>because</i> it's the &quot;time of Egyptomania&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, lucky for you!</div> </div> </div> </div>While being a history nerd. I really appreciate OP for making the Dark Eras book as I want to set my first Mummy game if I ever get to run it during this era. My idea is still very sketchy at the moment. But I know the opening scene will take place now during a ceremony to raise up a particular Mummy before the Sothic Cycle awakens her, will be a Mummy/Vampire crossover and starts with the flashback that sets the characters up in the 1920's in North Africa, though not specifically Egypt. I know I want it to involve the origins of the Mekhet but I haven't hashed out the details.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T09:35:20-08:00","id":324589,"title":"","content":"If it helps, I feel like the Strix are just as lovely antagonists for the Arisen as they are for the Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T12:35:25-08:00","id":324725,"title":"","content":"Oh man, you too?<br /> <br /> They're wonderful Lifeless to hunt... and be hunted by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-29T11:50:50-08:00","id":325458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/21622-when-have-you-set-your-mummy-the-curse-chronicles?p=324513#post324513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would complain that as the timeline goes that makes absolutely no sense (the first mummies woke up 1461 years, plus or minus a century, after the fall of the Nameless Empire).<br /> <br /> But that would be dumb, because you're doing something as awesome as <i>building the Indus Valley Civilization.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right?!<br /> <br /> Yeah, our ST doesn't give one whit about the official timeline, despite Mummy easily being his favourite NWoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T03:51:14-08:00","id":377092,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the necro, but I do so love this topic.<br /> <br /> I ran a one-shot set in the failed Egyptian coup of 1882, where one very amnesiac Desh Hry-Tp struggled to find out why she'd been executed in a previous Descent <i>and</i> fended off one nasty Shuankhsen-Amkhata duo as the city burned down around her. I'm considering further sessions in WW2's North Africa campaign and the Arab Spring, but I might start a new chronicle with additional players that explores the Third Turn and the Crusades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T11:32:21-08:00","id":377396,"title":"","content":"I'm running a game set in late 17th century Brazil. It hasn't progressed far enough to explore the interactions with other mummies, but &quot;Mummy and her cult looking for Eldorado&quot; seemed like a fun jumping-off point for a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"use